1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,683
The second attempt had a minimal requirement and a maximal ambition: one indoor session a week, provided the club could find a room.

2
00:00:08,683 --> 00:00:13,698
“We are not asking for a large provision,” Maya said.

3
00:00:13,698 --> 00:00:27,121
“We are asking for the series to exist.” A lucky student in a nearby suburb offered the hall of a skating club, and the nation of small habits began to take shape.

4
00:00:27,121 --> 00:00:31,386
The ratio of talk to movement was the first oddity.

5
00:00:31,386 --> 00:00:45,239
A nervous doctoral student measured the intake of sugar, the approximate intake of salt, and the proverbial intake of advice; the laughter that followed was genuine and slightly uneasy.

6
00:00:45,239 --> 00:00:56,432
“A fake plan and a conceptual one look identical on paper,” she said, “and only one of them survives contact with a suitcase.”

7
00:00:56,432 --> 00:01:05,541
The atmospheric part was harder: a windy suburb, an outer ring road, and a nightmare of bus connections.

8
00:01:05,541 --> 00:01:11,311
“Hospitality is not entertainment,” the easy-going coach said.

9
00:01:11,311 --> 00:01:24,254
“It is the interruption you do not mind.” A resemblance between the two approaches existed, but the inner one had vitality and the outer one had a poster.

10
00:01:24,254 --> 00:01:27,849
The prevention work was almost invisible.

11
00:01:27,849 --> 00:01:35,343
“An occurrence of injury is not a sexual matter and not a moral one,” the physiotherapist said.

12
00:01:35,343 --> 00:01:48,571
“It is an event with a date.” Arousal, sleepiness, and an amusing oddity in the data all pointed the same way: the second attempt had to be boring on purpose.

13
00:01:48,571 --> 00:01:53,810
The conceptual shift was to treat rest as part of the exercise.

14
00:01:53,810 --> 00:01:59,120
“An existent body is not a spherical one,” the coach said.

15
00:01:59,120 --> 00:02:16,678
“It has a history and a knee.” The sleepiness of the room at four o'clock, the smell of a conditioner bottle, and the sound of a distant match on the radio: all of it was the second attempt, and it was possibly the last one they would be given.

16
00:02:16,678 --> 00:02:24,597
The effort was especially difficult in the outskirts, where the music of the club never reached and a hot meal was a hit or a miss.

17
00:02:24,597 --> 00:02:40,685
“You watch a war of small habits,” the coach said, “and you are optimistic only because you are asleep.” The second attempt had to pass through those districts before it could call itself a programme.
